 {
  "primary": {
   "eyebrow_headline": [],
   "title": [
    {
     "type": "heading2",
     "text": "Kids Church FAQ's",
     "spans": []
    }
   ],
   "description": [],
   "optional_image": {}
  },
  "items": [
   {
    "question": "What is a Kids Life Group?",
    "answer": [
     {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "In some locations, we run mid-week life groups for kids and families. Our Life Group leaders gather families together to have fun, go deeper in their faith and to celebrate what it means to live a Christian life.",
      "spans": [],
      "direction": "ltr"
     },
     {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "\nEmail kids@thec3.uk to find a Life Group near you.",
      "spans": [
       {
        "start": 7,
        "end": 20,
        "type": "hyperlink",
        "data": {
         "link_type": "Web",
         "url": "mailto:kids@thec3.uk",
         "target": "_blank"
        }
       }
      ],
      "direction": "ltr"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "question": "What is Champions Club?",
    "answer": [
     {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Champions Club Leaders exist to serve kids with additional needs during Kids Church. We want to do all we can to partner with you so that your kids can flourish in our church family. Champions Club support can be arranged in advance of Sunday services. To enquire about 1-2-1 support for your child in Kids Church, please get in touch here.",
      "spans": [
       {
        "start": 335,
        "end": 339,
        "type": "hyperlink",
        "data": {
         "id": "YnWB3xAAACIAoFXW",
         "type": "page",
         "tags": [
          "domain:thec3.uk"
         ],
         "lang": "en-gb",
         "slug": "get-in-touch",
         "first_publication_date": "2022-05-06T20:19:17+0000",
         "last_publication_date": "2025-10-24T22:07:02+0000",
         "uid": "contact",
         "link_type": "Document",
         "isBroken": false
        }
       }
      ]
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "question": "What do you teach at Kids Church?",
    "answer": [
     {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "We create the majority of our teaching content for C3 Kids in house. Teaching is always age appropriate and Bible-based. We design our sessions to include worship, an interactive Bible message, with creative prayer and activities. We aim to help your child grow in their spiritual, emotional and social development. Our aim is for your child to leave a Kids Church service having had fun with friends and with their hearts full of faith.",
      "spans": [],
      "direction": "ltr"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "question": "How do I check-in my child to Kids Church?",
    "answer": [
     {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "When you arrive at church for the first time, our team will direct you to the relevant Kids Church settings. We use a database called ChurchSuite to register all of our C3 Kids.",
      "spans": [],
      "direction": "ltr"
     },
     {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": " You will be asked to provide emergency contact details and details for the kids you are registering (including full name, date of birth and relevant medical/dietary information). ",
      "spans": [],
      "direction": "ltr"
     },
     {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "After registering, you will be given a name label for your child to wear during Kids Church and a guardian pick-up label for you to collect your child at the end of the session. ",
      "spans": [],
      "direction": "ltr"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "question": "How do the C3 Kids Team ensure my child is safe at Kids Church?",
    "answer": [
     {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Our C3 Kids Leaders are DBS checked and go through an onboarding process including safer recruitment practices such as character reference checks to serve in Kids Church. We ensure our safeguarding policies are regularly reviewed and that our team are trained and reminded to serve within the guidelines of our safeguarding policy.",
      "spans": [],
      "direction": "ltr"
     },
     {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "\nIf we need to contact you during the service, our team will text or phone the emergency contact number you provided during registration. A team member may also come into the auditorium to reach you if needed. If an evacuation was needed our team would respond calmly and quickly, taking the children to the Kids Evacuation Point. They will then take a register before releasing the children back to their guardian to ensure all children are accounted for.",
      "spans": [],
      "direction": "ltr"
     }
    ]
   }
  ],
  "id": "faq_section$85e7e722-ca89-468b-ba73-cef87282daaf",
  "slice_type": "faq_section",
  "slice_label": null
